This script also includes the `CHECKPOINT` command. When the recovery model of your database is Simple, this command helps to not grow log file size.

If your database is in Full Recovery Model, instead of `CHECKPOINT`, regularly execute `BACKUP LOG` command on your database. This backups the transaction log and marks the portion of the log file as ready for reuse, which helps prevent growth of the log file. Do remember, though, that shrinking the files will have a cost in performance next time SQL Server needs to increase the file size, so monitor your autogrowth settings accordingly.

